{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779564515,"nonce":"IvrhiA28SqbiS16kP28vXoOt3qA=","message":"## Retained-observable rescope from `07c0ec9` audit\n\nThe graph-template umbrella changes the implementation direction for this issue. The current title still says probe/metric nodes, but the audit confirms the durable core contract should be retained observables rather than default graph nodes.\n\nCurrent confirmed state:\n\n- Provider schema enumeration already exposes selector targets for ports, task data, objectives, probes, runtime sample leaves, and curated state hints.\n- Probe state is fragmented: `TapSpec`, legacy `BarnacleSpec`, untyped `StudioScenarioSpec.probe_specs`, implicit port probes from `loss_service`, and frontend “Add probe here” behavior that creates loss terms rather than durable retained probes.\n- Objective/loss lowering still drops too much semantic information. `StudioObjectiveTermSpec` has source/target/value/temporal selectors, but lowering to `LossTermSpec` mostly preserves only a single `selector`, norm, and time aggregation.\n- Runtime retention is still mostly full `state_history` by default, with a streaming-loss path that is not driven by Studio objective/probe specs.\n- Loss/analysis code still assumes SimpleFeedback-style state views such as `states.mechanics`, `states.net`, and `states.efferent`.\n\nConcrete contract to implement under this issue after the first graph-template slice:\n\n1. Add typed retained observable specs with target kinds: `port`, `edge`, `graph_output`, `recurrent_carry`, `state_path`, and `task_data`.\n2. Add explicit retention policies: `stream`, `window` with size/order, and `trajectory`.\n3. Make selector schema metadata advertise the retention target and default retention policy for ports, graph outputs, edges, recurrent carries, and explicit probes.\n4. Make Studio “Add probe” write durable retained-observable specs, not a loss term.\n5. Lower objective/loss specs to a retention plan and fail pathfully if a selected transient value cannot be streamed or retained.\n6. Extend rollout/eval/training artifacts with retained-observable outputs; do not store every port by default.\n7. Replace SimpleFeedback-state hardcoded hints with explicit graph/template state selectors as graph execution becomes canonical.\n\nThe `feature/graph-templates` branch is adding the first typed spec surface now so future losses/Studio Data projection have a durable target, but the full execution/artifact pipeline remains follow-up work on this issue unless it becomes necessary to complete the graph-template runtime change.","files":null}]}